[node name="pine4m" parent="Pine_4m/Pine_4m_root" index="0"]
; pine-leaf, not pine-branch: the mesh is one combined surface covering the
; whole tree (see the build comment on Pine_4m.fbx's own broken material
; mapping), and most of a pine's silhouette is needle mass, not bark — using
; the bark-brown branch texture across the whole tree made it read as a
; near-black blob. Leaf is a proper alpha-cutout needle card texture; the
; small trunk portion at the base shows needle texture rather than bark as a
; result, which is the accepted tradeoff.
;
; ShaderMaterial rather than StandardMaterial3D from here on — see
; tree_sway.gdshader — because wind response needs a custom vertex function,
; which StandardMaterial3D cannot run.
material_override = ExtResource("2")

